WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.567
-That's right, everybody.
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.534
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.200
You're here. Big show.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.701
Big show tonight.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.033
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.901
Keith Richards
is my guest tonight.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:19.033
♪♪

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.501
I am such a huge fan.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.067
I went up to Keith backstage,
I told him, "You are my hero.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.200
The Stones are the greatest
rock 'n' roll band ever,"

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.033
and I'll never, never forget
what Keith told me.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.968
He said...
[ Mumbling quietly ]

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.501
It was so heartfelt.
Yeah, I love it.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:34.968
I'm so glad Keith is here,
actually.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.167
It makes me so happy
because it's rained now

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.968
seven weekends in a row here
in New York City.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.434
Everything is soaked.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.501
The rain is so bad that today,
on my way into work,

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.501
I saw a squirrel rubbing
talcum powder on his nuts.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.133
And I go, "That's when it's..."

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.901
-Acorns?
-Well, guys, some big news.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:56.334
Last night, President Biden gave
a national prime-time address

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:58.601
about what's happening
in Israel and Ukraine.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:01.234
And people are saying it's the
best speech he's ever given.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:02.467
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.167
Yeah, this might have been
Biden's best speech

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.801
since he opened for Lincoln
at Gettysburg.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:07.834
They --
-Oy!

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.300
-That's right.
Biden proved two

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.267
very important things
to the world --

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:14.033
that we will stand
with our allies

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.434
and that he can stay
awake past 8:00 p.m.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.801
That's -- that's it.
He did it.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:23.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.767
That's right.
Biden's speech pre-empted

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.667
all the network's
regular programming,

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:29.167
so people tuning in were like,

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.434
"This is the most boring episode
of 'The Golden Bachelor' yet."

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:35.133
Some more news
from Washington.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:39.434
After losing the speaker vote
for the third time this week --

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.968
the third time, yeah --
Congressman Jim Jordan

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.934
is no longer in the running
for speaker of the House.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:49.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.934
Well, he was never
in the running.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:53.801
Now he's officially
not in the running.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.434
But get this --
the temporary speaker,

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:59.434
Congressman Patrick McHenry,
is around 5'5", okay?

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:00.968
And some people noticed
that he seemed

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:05.067
to swap out the speaker's chair
to make himself look taller.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.367
Here's the old chair.
You see this? Yeah.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.567
Now, this is real.
Here's the new one.

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:14.100
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.234
I thought this was nice.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.868
They also added a set
of those dog steps

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.934
so we can reach the podium.
I thought that was nice.

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.734
Guys, I read that
former president Trump

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:25.334
was just fined $5,000
for violating a gag order

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.601
in his New York
civil fraud trial.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:30.767
Even more concerning,
Trump was like, "I'm ruined!"

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.868
[ Muted cymbal crash ]

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.267
Guys, some business news.
Today, Spirit Airlines

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.100
canceled dozens of flights

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.334
to perform a "necessary"
inspection of the planes.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:47.667
So, until now, I guess

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.467
they considered
inspections optional?

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.667
Is that -- "Necessary?"

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.567
I'm not sure
what's more stressful --

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.133
being on one of the flights
that was canceled

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.300
or one of the flights
that wasn't.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.534
You're like, "Wait."

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.234
Honestly, I always thought
a Spirit inspection

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:00.834
was just a guy coming out
and kicking the tires

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.133
like -- [ Inhales sharply ] --
"It's good."

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.868
[ Laughter ]
"Fly."

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.934
Well, listen to this.
After an FDA panel found

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:11.968
that an ingredient in cold
medicines like Mucinex, NyQuil,

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:14.434
and Sudafed
doesn't actually work,

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.033
CVS announced
that they are pulling

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.300
some of the medicines
from their shelves.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.567
Yep, so now Sudafed's
entire demographic

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.067
is people making meth.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:26.467
[ Laughter ]
That's it.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.200
Well, this is going viral.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.901
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:32.267
"Can I get a key to the --
Yeah."

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.133
This is going viral.
An international student

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:36.334
was applying for colleges
in the U.S.

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:38.567
and wanted to go
to the University of Miami

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:39.701
to be near the beach,

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:42.167
but she accidentally
enrolled in Miami, Ohio.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.467
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:44.601
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:45.968
She also meant
to apply to Brown,

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.801
but now she has a job at UPS.
-Oh.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:51.367
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.000
[ Scattered applause ]

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.000
So it's like -- Yeah.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.434
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.000
[ Applause ]

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.534
And finally, a new study found

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:01.000
that sitting in a hot tub
for 30 minutes

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.601
has the same health benefits
as going for a run.

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:09.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:13.000
That -- That is according
to the new head of the CDC,

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.634
Dr. Tommy Bahama.
We have a great show.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.734
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:26.467
♪♪

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.667
Wh-a-a-a-a-at?!

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:36.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.801
"Hackney Diamonds" is out now.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.968
The new Rolling Stones
album is out now.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:46.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.801
And he is on our show tonight.

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:51.467
Last night,
I was very, very lucky.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:54.634
I got invited to the --
to a secret show, actually.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.100
I went to the album --
It was the album --

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.200
What do they call it?
-Release.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.667
-A release party.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.801
I go, "Great. I'll go to see
the album release party to see,

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:05.100
you know, Mick and Ronnie
and Keith are there."

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.534
I go, "Great."
I go, "Are they playing?"

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.367
They go, "No, no, no, no, no.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.901
No, it's just
an album release party."

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.267
"Okay, cool."
I go, "Well, that's fine.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.567
I'll just go."

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.133
And then I saw you,
and you go -- you're D.J.'ing.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.634
-Yeah.
-And you're there, so I go,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.334
"Oh, cool. That'll be fun.
I'll see Quest.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.701
It'll be fun to go out there."

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.667
I go in there.
It's a tiny club.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:24.400
Tiny.
Where was it? Racket?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.634
-Racket.
-On 16th Street, I remember.

00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:28.734
It's a beautiful club
but small.

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.434
But there's instruments
on stage.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:31.167
-Oh.
-Ooh.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.567
-There's a drum set.

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:35.901
There's guitars.
There's a microphone.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:39.100
I go, "Uh-oh. I think
something's gonna go down."

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.200
All of a sudden,
the lights go out.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.834
Questlove's
not D.J.'ing anymore.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.133
He's sitting where I'm sitting.
I go, "Dude, what's happening?"

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:46.734
You're like, "Oh, yeah,
it's about to go down."

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.300
They come out,
and it's almost like

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:52.300
♪ Shadow, shadow ♪

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.901
I was like, "What?"
It was unbelievable.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.067
I was -- honestly, I think --
I'm not kidding.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:01.033
I don't want to complain.
I think I was too close.

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:03.667
-Yeah.
-Do you think we were too close?

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.767
-That'll never happen
in our lifetime again.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:08.567
-I was too close to the Stones.
-Wow.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.968
-I think it was
a little distracting.

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:12.434
-Like, how close?
-Well, like,

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:13.801
say I'm here, right?

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.267
This is me.
-Right.

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:17.100
-And he's like --

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.534
And he's like, "Go away,
go away, go away.

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:19.968
[ Gibberish ]

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.501
"Go, go! Stop! Go!
Move out of the way!"

00:06:21.501 --> 00:06:24.133
Like, he couldn't --
I was ruining his mojo.

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:26.467
Mick was out
doing his thing, and...

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:27.701
And I was just like --

00:06:27.701 --> 00:06:30.200
I was just, like,
sitting, like...

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.534
I was getting --

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:33.400
I was getting a lap dance
from Mick Jagger.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.868
I don't do that.
-Yeah.

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:40.734
-I don't do that.
But it happened last night.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.801
It was unbelievable.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:45.801
And they came out, and they just
showed everybody how you do it,

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:48.367
which is like, no tricks,
no computers, no anything.

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:49.767
"Give me a guitar,
give me a microphone.

00:06:49.767 --> 00:06:51.167
I'm gonna show you
how to rock out."

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:54.467
And they destroyed.
They were so great.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:57.767
And at the end, they finish,
and they -- they leave.

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:59.934
And, you know, I don't know
if there's such a thing

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:02.367
as encores anymore.
Not really, right?

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:04.200
You kind of know
they're coming out for one more.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.367
They have to.
Right?

00:07:05.367 --> 00:07:07.534
The lights turn on,
and you go -- we go home.

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:10.968
Back in the day,
you have to go, "One more..."

00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:12.801
They don't do that anymore.
I'm fine with that.

00:07:12.801 --> 00:07:14.534
So I'm playing the game.
I go, "Yeah,"

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.234
but I can --
I can see the lights aren't on,

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:18.200
so they're gonna come out
for one more.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.634
Not only do they come out
for one more,

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:23.067
Lady Gaga comes out
with The Rolling Stones.

00:07:23.067 --> 00:07:28.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:30.767
I mean, all-timer performance.
-Yes.

00:07:30.767 --> 00:07:32.534
-All-timer performance.
-Yeah.

00:07:32.534 --> 00:07:35.234
-Everybody --
Keith was on fire.

00:07:35.234 --> 00:07:37.033
Literally.
Someone lit him on fire.

00:07:37.033 --> 00:07:39.934
He was like -- he just played --
He was awesome.

00:07:39.934 --> 00:07:42.234
Ronnie Wood and Gaga
just went for it.

00:07:42.234 --> 00:07:44.534
Rock 'n' roll.
It was unbelievable.

00:07:44.534 --> 00:07:46.601
All the new songs
they played, it's great.

00:07:46.601 --> 00:07:49.701
Anyways, "Hackney Diamonds"
is out officially today.

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:52.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.701
On our show.

00:07:54.701 --> 00:07:57.834
He is one of the greatest
guitarists of all time

00:07:57.834 --> 00:07:59.267
in one of the greatest
bands of all time,

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:00.501
The Rolling Stones.

00:08:00.501 --> 00:08:02.234
New album, "Hackney Diamonds,"
is out now.

00:08:02.234 --> 00:08:03.734
He is here with us tonight.

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:07.467
Keith Richards is on the show
tonight, so that'll be fun.

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:09.501
That'll be cool to see, Keith.
That'll be great.

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:11.267
But we'll get to Keith...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:20.634
♪♪

00:08:20.634 --> 00:08:22.767
Not now. Later.

00:08:22.767 --> 00:08:24.934
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:08:24.934 --> 00:08:29.968
♪♪

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:31.467
-That was a walk-by.

00:08:31.467 --> 00:08:33.200
-Not now.
-Yeah.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.767
-He will be on the show,
but not -- not yet.

00:08:35.767 --> 00:08:42.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.868
How cool is that dude
right there?

00:08:43.868 --> 00:08:45.968
He just --
you know, just walk out.

00:08:45.968 --> 00:08:47.801
[ Applause ]

00:08:47.801 --> 00:08:49.267
He doesn't care.
He's Keith Richards.

00:08:49.267 --> 00:08:51.767
He does what he wants.

00:08:51.767 --> 00:08:53.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.934 --> 00:08:56.000
Plus, they are
Grammy-winning artists

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.133
who have sold over
45 million albums combined.

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:02.434
Their new album,
"Welcome 2 ColleGrove,"

00:09:02.434 --> 00:09:04.367
comes out November 17th,

00:09:04.367 --> 00:09:07.367
2 Chainz and Lil Wayne
are here tonight.

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:09.234
We're going to talk to them,

00:09:09.234 --> 00:09:12.467
and then they're performing
later in the show.

00:09:12.467 --> 00:09:16.968
It's a big show tonight.
2 Chainz and Lil Wayne.

00:09:16.968 --> 00:09:19.000
Guys, today is Friday,
and that's usually

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.868
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:09:20.868 --> 00:09:23.267
I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:24.701
and, of course,
I send out Thank You Notes.

00:09:24.701 --> 00:09:25.968
I like to write out
Thank You Notes.

00:09:25.968 --> 00:09:28.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Don't we do --

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.167
I'd like to write out some
weekly Thank You Notes

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:31.667
right now for you guys.
Do you guys mind

00:09:31.667 --> 00:09:32.767
if I write some out tonight?

00:09:32.767 --> 00:09:34.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:36.367
I appreciate it!

00:09:36.367 --> 00:09:39.067
James, can I get some Thank
You Note writing music, please?

00:09:39.067 --> 00:09:41.834
♪♪

00:09:41.834 --> 00:09:43.234
Wow.
-He's not in his wig.

00:09:43.234 --> 00:09:44.601
-Yeah, he's in a good mood.

00:09:44.601 --> 00:09:46.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:51.567
I like his shirt.
-Yeah. It's classy.

00:09:51.567 --> 00:09:53.067
-Yeah, it's like --
It's like a rust color.

00:09:53.067 --> 00:09:54.834
-Yeah. Let's see it again.

00:09:54.834 --> 00:09:57.567
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:09:57.567 --> 00:09:59.968
That's beautiful, man.
He's called "Mr. Autumn."

00:09:59.968 --> 00:10:02.467
-Yeah.
Mr. Autumn, they call him. Yeah.

00:10:02.467 --> 00:10:03.801
-That's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.801 --> 00:10:05.467
-His shirts change
like the leaves.

00:10:05.467 --> 00:10:07.000
-Yeah.
-It's a beautiful thing.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.234
-Only once a year.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:10:10.234 --> 00:10:11.634
That's the same shirt he wore --

00:10:11.634 --> 00:10:14.200
-Same shirt he wore last autumn.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.634
-It just progressively
gets filthy.

00:10:15.634 --> 00:10:17.667
-It's from the fall collection.
-Yeah. Until it falls off.

00:10:17.667 --> 00:10:19.033
-Yeah.
-And then he's shirtless.

00:10:19.033 --> 00:10:21.434
And then he shirtless.
-Get threadbare until it falls.

00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:23.300
And then we know
the times have changed.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.300
You know what I mean?
-That's the only way I know

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.100
that I'm alive, is to
